{"event_type":"review","id":"b8d27645f03e48e9cdc15d11970ef2263e6382991f754b2dd4ca3fb754ea591c","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T20:16:34Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/73376d8907b070300e76c20a983a1a704267058ff97d06ed55fa21a7b19755c5","sha256":"73376d8907b070300e76c20a983a1a704267058ff97d06ed55fa21a7b19755c5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7edbf4abba3ff0d1e5960bdcad95e5e1489ae1a825b1463c7d99f2f24bf0faef","sha256":"7edbf4abba3ff0d1e5960bdcad95e5e1489ae1a825b1463c7d99f2f24bf0faef"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/739736b948e98b52d883983818c50b5cef15ab680f6c547e3be9b6dbfdb8c6ef","sha256":"739736b948e98b52d883983818c50b5cef15ab680f6c547e3be9b6dbfdb8c6ef"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e7c5761e4af510f0415b3949b7e3cf0e81d3935f367c4d146f7a858bbe24463c","sha256":"e7c5761e4af510f0415b3949b7e3cf0e81d3935f367c4d146f7a858bbe24463c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/505632321d4ac3f75e394c126de0320b08828075f2ce122b003eb2d35dbd2f1e","sha256":"505632321d4ac3f75e394c126de0320b08828075f2ce122b003eb2d35dbd2f1e"}],"attempt_id":"82391641c11ac74bbe60918d9baaddcc631d30a489e28d8464e2c0a5c28f588d:0:1","base":"45e07d27acddffbef3b19444d38f5c1408fd8436","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"d6e56b8e405be2bdff025d4d63b4c2c69e6d4672","body":"**Verify that `deletedAtHead` handles unusual file names.**\n\nscripts/lib/owned-files.mjs:15-19. `git ls-tree --name-only` quotes paths with special characters, such as non-ASCII bytes, tabs, quotes, and newlines. This happens when `core.quotePath` is on, which is the default. The quoted output never equals `rel`, so a valid tracked deletion is rejected.\n\nAdd `-z` and split on `\\0` to avoid this.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  const result = spawnSync('git', ['ls-tree', '--name-only', 'HEAD', '--', rel], {\n+  const result = spawnSync('git', ['ls-tree', '-z', '--name-only', 'HEAD', '--', rel], {\n...\n-  return result.status === 0 && result.stdout.split('\\n').includes(rel);\n+  return result.status === 0 && result.stdout.split('\\0').includes(rel);\n```\n</details>","id":"96b09fc9f3bca7f29341e685145f848d56ef7173a68bf8f66d18cba7fcb1e687","intervals":[],"path":"scripts/lib/owned-files.mjs","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Verify that `deletedAtHead` handles unusual file names."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"24a5d42360999d3d32c8104b81d15c1e60391ac7","body":"**Correct the report type description.**\n\n`src/kernel/README.md:108` says `RunEarlyStopReason` contains only `'budget'`. The type and schema also allow `'signal'`, and the runner can return it. Consumers may reject a valid signal report if they follow the outdated statement.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- `stopOnError` leaving jobs unstarted does NOT set `stoppedEarly`: the\n-  frozen `RunEarlyStopReason` only contains `'budget'`, and honest-stop\n-  marking is T1.3's — callers read `counts.queued`/`counts.blocked` to see\n-  what never ran.\n+- `stopOnError` alone does not set `stoppedEarly`. Callers read\n+  `counts.queued`/`counts.blocked` to see what never ran. The frozen\n+  `RunEarlyStopReason` contains `'budget'` and `'signal'`.\n```\n\n</details>","id":"374bb3ff764861cce14538912e4ee87144bf684d2c9118626122e249604cbdf6","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/README.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Correct the report type description."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"24a5d42360999d3d32c8104b81d15c1e60391ac7","body":"**Distinguish reservation-era cost folds.**\n\n`src/kernel/README.md:512-516` says runs with reservations fold cost from reservation events, including unresolved reservations. Qualify the earlier statement so operators do not expect a crashed dispatch to have no charge.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  the dispatch count and the usage/`costUSD` rollups seed from\n-  job-finished events (a finish counts only when it CLOSES an open start),\n+  the dispatch count and usage rollups seed from job-finished events\n+  (a finish counts only when it CLOSES an open start). The `costUSD` rollup\n+  seeds from reservation events for runs with reservations and from\n+  job-finished events otherwise,\n```\n\n</details>","id":"18d4cda7624c6790b632a49bf7f39c3b50aab94c2bee7643c6797ca70efe4ed5","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/README.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Distinguish reservation-era cost folds."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"24a5d42360999d3d32c8104b81d15c1e60391ac7","body":"**Do not claim the full charge covers post-settle spend.**\n\nIn `src/kernel/README.md:439-440`, the full charge is based on the reservation and evidence folded before settlement. A detached op can spend more afterward, and its late evidence cannot trigger a breach. Document this limit; the following normal-settle residual describes a different case.","id":"39381d6aeb8a23717edc5c091b91c3b1284a61091c4e50626c55f26b957c89c5","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/README.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not claim the full charge covers post-settle spend."}],"head":"e6ffb709b377d1ca350c8890e73db64c808bb393","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"af8ae86ed2a303eb2a28201efefbf295b0a16e61","intervals":[[16,16],[19,19],[49,49],[51,51],[55,62],[94,95],[99,99],[108,110],[122,125],[151,154],[170,170],[177,178],[189,189],[192,192],[198,199],[201,203],[259,259],[262,266],[285,285],[290,296],[335,335],[361,362],[365,366],[377,377],[381,383],[386,388],[398,399],[427,428],[446,448],[460,462]],"path":"scripts/dd1-abort-spike.mjs"},{"blob":"d